## 2. Dataset Reality: The "Three Folders" Demystified

The provided archive at `data/track_2/documents/` contains two core components:

```text
data/track_2/documents/
├── daily_drilling_reports/
│   ├── Daily_Drilling_Report___HTML_Version/   (32 files)
│   ├── Daily_Drilling_Report___PDF_Version/    (32 files)
│   └── Daily_Drilling_Report___XML_Version/    (32 files)  <-- OUR CORE ENGINE
│
└── wellbore_files/                             (180 files: 70 PDFs, 110 survey files)
```

### Key Architectural Insights:
1. **The Three DDR Folders are identical:** The HTML, PDF, and XML folders contain the **exact same 32 daily drilling reports** exported in three formats from Equinor's historical Volve database.
2. **XML is our superpower:** WITSML XML is already 100% structured data. It eliminates OCR errors, messy HTML parsing, and external parsing dependencies. Built-in `xml.etree.ElementTree` ingests all 32 reports into memory in **0.034 seconds**.
3. **The Role of `wellbore_files`:** Contains final post-drill well summaries and survey coordinate listings. All 24 answerable open-test questions target hourly operations, mud checks, and daily report dates that live exclusively inside the Daily Drilling Reports.

